Note: Keith's ICARUS simulations from his email of 11/22/10
Note: (1) blizzard : snowflake :: army : soldier   (cross-domain, slow "true")
Note: (2) blizzard : snowflake :: monsoon : raindrop (within-domain, fast "true")
Note: (3) blizzard : snowflake :: tornado : cloud (false)
Note: Approach is to use LISA's similarity engine to do this: Can analog MIP similarity serve as an index of analogy validity?
Note: This sym file implements analogy 2 above

Analog snow
  DefPreds
    part_of 2 part whole disorganized unstructured natural ;
  end { defpreds
  DefObjs
    snowflake weather water snow small ice crystal ;
    blizzard weather water snow storm much large dangerous ;
  end { defobjs
  DefProps
    P1 part_of ( snowflake blizzard ) ;
  end { defprops
Done { analog 0

Analog rain
  DefPreds
    part_of 2 part whole disorganized unstructured natural ;
  end { defpreds
  DefObjs
    raindrop weather water rain small drop wet ;
    monsoon weather water rain storm much large dangerous ;
  end { defobjs
  DefProps
    P1 part_of ( raindrop monsoon ) ;
  end { defprops
Done { analog 0

Sequence
  Driver=[ 0 ] { set analog 0 to driver
  Recip=[ 1 ] { set analog 1 to recip
  { sim_on means turn similarity calculation on 
  Order=[ sim_on P1 h ]
Done.
